from h34 import *
M=mcq;F=tf;S=short;N=num
chapter(4,'english','maheshwar','Maheshwar',
 ('A fort built by a queen','Aarav and Ananya see a picture of a grand fort in the newspaper, and their Chachi tells them about Maheshwar Fort, built by Queen Ahilya Bai on the banks of the Narmada River. In this chapter you will read the conversation, learn words like majestic and overhanging, find words with similar meanings, spot silent letters, use the articles a, an and the, and read about the famous Maheshwari sarees.'),
 [('The picture in the newspaper',['One pleasant evening Aarav and Ananya sat with their Chachi, their paternal aunt, and saw a picture of a grand fort in the newspaper.','Chachi told them it was the majestic Maheshwar Fort, built long ago by Queen Ahilya Bai.','The fort is famous for its overhanging balconies, which seem to float in the air.','Aarav and Ananya were excited to learn that a real queen had built it.']),
  ('Queen Ahilya Bai',['Queen Ahilya Bai ruled Maheshwar in Madhya Pradesh, about 95 kilometres from Indore. She was a warrior queen and belonged to the great Holkar family.','She had the fort built on a hill on the banks of the Narmada River, so that she could see her whole kingdom. It is also called Ahilya Fort.','She protected her people and built temples, schools and wells. She ruled with kindness and wisdom, and people loved her.','A thirteen-feet tall statue of the queen stands in front of the palace even today, like a guardian watching over her land.']),
  ('The fort and the town',['The fort is known for its unique style of construction and its grand staircases.','It was built with special red stones brought from Gujarat and Rajasthan.','It stands on a hill, with the town of Maheshwar on one side and the Narmada River on the other, and many beautifully designed temples are near it.','Aarav and Ananya promised to visit one day with Chachi to discover its secrets.']),
  ('Maheshwari sarees',['The people of Maheshwar are known for weaving the famous Maheshwari sarees.','They were first made of pure silk, but later cotton yarn was introduced, and then a blend of cotton and silk became popular.','As they gained popularity, the handloom weaving tradition began in Maheshwar.','These sarees are famous for their unique reversible borders and pallus, in colours such as peacock blue, bright yellow, forest green and an Indian red dye called Aal.','Today they are sold in India and in other countries.']),
  ('New words',['A fort is a strong building built for defence. Majestic means grand and impressive.','Overhanging means sticking out over something below. Balconies are platforms that stick out from the wall of a building.','A ruler is a person who governs a country. Unique means one of its kind, special.']),
  ('Similar words and odd one out',['Words with similar meanings are synonyms. Happy, joyful and cheerful are similar. Brave, bold and fearless are similar.','In sad, unhappy, tearful and thrilled, thrilled is the odd one out because it is happy.','In talk, discuss, kind and speak, kind is the odd one out because it is not about speaking.','In noisy, quiet, silent and calm, noisy is the odd one out because the others are about peace.','In cotton, wooden, silk and woollen, wooden is the odd one out because the others are fabrics.']),
  ('Silent letters and word meanings',['In design the letter g is silent. In sign, high, light, night, sing and king, the g is silent in sign, light, night and high, but not in sing and king or goat, sugar and magnet.','Match the qualities: kindness is being kind, bravery is being brave, wisdom is being wise, majestic is being royal, unique is being special, fierce is being strong and dedicated is being devoted.']),
  ('Articles a, an and the',['A and an are used for one of something not named before, and the is used for a particular thing.','Once upon a time, there lived a monkey on an oak tree.','We use an before a vowel sound, as in an apple, an old man and an olive.','We use the when we mean something specific: It gave the pear to an elephant means that particular pear.','The naughty monkey snatched the bag. The dog found the apple and stole it.']),
  ('Presenting a historical place',['Ask elders about a historical place near you.','In your presentation say the name of the place and the monument, the historical people connected with it, its special features, how people feel about it and other facts.','You can also make a fort puzzle: draw a fort on thick paper, cut it into pieces and put it together again.'])],
 [('Fill in a, an or the: Once upon ___ time, there lived ___ monkey on ___ oak tree.',[('Time is the first noun, a time we do not name exactly.','Once upon a time is a fixed phrase.'),('Monkey starts with a consonant sound, so a monkey.','A goes before consonant sounds.'),('Oak starts with a vowel sound, so an oak tree.','An goes before vowel sounds.')]),
  ('Which word is the odd one out: cotton, wooden, silk, woollen?',[('Cotton, silk and woollen are fabrics.','They are made into clothes.'),('Wooden is made of wood.','It is not a fabric.'),('So wooden is the odd one out.','Look for what most words have in common.')])],
 ('Tell about Maheshwar Fort and Queen Ahilya Bai in your own words.',['A fort on a hill by the Narmada built by Queen Ahilya Bai','Overhanging balconies and grand staircases','Red stones from Gujarat and Rajasthan','Maheshwari sarees of cotton and silk'],['The fort was built by a king in Delhi','The fort is in Tamil Nadu']),
 ['Queen Ahilya Bai of the Holkar family built Maheshwar Fort on the Narmada.','The fort has overhanging balconies and red stones from Gujarat and Rajasthan.','Maheshwari sarees are made of cotton and silk.','A and an are used for one thing, and the points to a particular thing.','Words with similar meanings help us find the odd one out.'],
 [M('1',1,'Who was Ahilya Bai?','A warrior queen of the Holkar family who ruled Maheshwar',[('A weaver','She was a queen'),('A teacher','She was a queen')],'She built the fort.'),
  M('2',1,'Where is Maheshwar Fort?','On a hill by the Narmada River in Madhya Pradesh',[('On an island','It is on a hill'),('In Kerala','It is in Madhya Pradesh')],'It overlooks the town and the river.'),
  M('3',1,'What material was used to build the fort?','Special red stones from Gujarat and Rajasthan',[('White marble','Red stones'),('Wood','Red stones')],'The stones were brought from two states.'),
  M('4',1,'What does the statue of Ahilya Bai represent?','A guardian watching over her land',[('A soldier','A guardian'),('A weaver','A guardian')],'It stands in front of the palace.'),
  M('5',1,'What are Maheshwari sarees made from?','Cotton and silk',[('Only wool','Cotton and silk'),('Jute','Cotton and silk')],'They were first pure silk.'),
  M('6',2,'What does majestic mean?','Grand and impressive',[('Small','Not the meaning'),('Broken','Not the meaning')],'The fort looks grand.'),
  M('7',2,'What does overhanging mean?','Sticking out over something below',[('Falling down','Not the meaning'),('Very old','Not the meaning')],'The balconies stick out.'),
  M('8',2,'Which word is the odd one out: sad, unhappy, tearful, thrilled?','thrilled',[('sad','Sad matches the group'),('tearful','Tearful matches the group')],'Thrilled means very happy.'),
  M('9',2,'Which word has a silent g?','Sign',[('Goat','The g is heard'),('Sugar','The g is heard')],'Sign sounds like sine.'),
  M('10',2,'Fill in: Once upon ___ time','a',[('an','Time starts with a consonant sound'),('the','Not used in this phrase')],'Once upon a time.'),
  F('11',2,'The statue of Queen Ahilya Bai is thirteen feet tall.',True,'It stands in front of the palace.'),
  S('12',3,'Which river flows by Maheshwar Fort?',['narmada','the narmada','narmada river'],'The fort is on the Narmada.')],
 keep=['Maheshwar','Narmada'])
